<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Calametra.Domain — what the business is.

    HARD RULE: no <ProjectReference> ever.
    SINGLE PERMITTED PACKAGE: NetTopologySuite.

    NetTopologySuite is a pure geometry value-type library: no I/O, no database,
    no framework, no provider SDK. Calametra's domain is inherently geospatial —
    an event's epicentre and a hazard's extent ARE domain concepts. Excluding
    geometry types would push those concepts out of the domain, which damages the
    architecture more than the package reference does.

    This is the same class of deliberate trade the reference template makes for
    EF Core in the Application layer (design_3 §10 Option A).

    Enforced by Calametra.ArchitectureTests:
      Domain_ShouldHaveNoProjectReferences
      Domain_ShouldOnlyReferenceNetTopologySuite
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NetTopologySuite" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
